  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "The word decline sounds terrifying. But when economists use it about America, they mostly mean something boring. Arithmetic.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "globe",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "chartDown"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Decline?",
            "Just arithmetic."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "If your share of the world was forty percent and everyone else grows faster, your share must fall. Even if you're thriving.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "kicker": "the math",
          "line": "Share must fall",
          "sub": "when others grow faster"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That catch-up growth is economic convergence, and it's expected.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-conv",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · convergence"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "America can keep getting richer in absolute terms while its slice of the global pie gets thinner.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "richer",
          "label": "yet a smaller share",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "globe"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A country can remain a leading great power with a smaller relative share.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-greatpower",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · great power"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "What actually changes is leverage. When you're one big player among several, you can't dictate terms alone.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Less leverage",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "That's the shift to a multipolar world, power shared among many.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-multipolar",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · multipolarity"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So collapse and relative decline are completely different things, even if the headlines blur them.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "center",
          "art": "globe",
          "line": "Not the same thing",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "check"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Same country, a smaller slice of the pie, and people confuse the two constantly.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Smaller slice",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So, does the word decline still scare you?",
